      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re probably right, but I think that\u0027s how the API has always behaved. Digging into the code we do something that makes sense in the validate_token method, which is wrap the call to validate the token with a try/except. If we catch an Unauthorized, we raise a Not Found [0]. But in other parts of token validation, when we go to validate the project information, we raise a 404 Project Not Found if the project doesn\u0027t exist [1]. Since they are both 404s, I wonder if we can raise a 401 in the cases where the project or identity provider doesn\u0027t exist and trade that for a 404 Token Not Found instead.\n\nThought?\n\n[0] https://github.com/openstack/keystone/blob/d3818f05e31729ac86415d6f114f658d98a704ab/keystone/token/provider.py#L146-L161\n[1] https://github.com/openstack/keystone/blob/d3818f05e31729ac86415d6f114f658d98a704ab/keystone/token/providers/common.py#L138-L143",
